1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,474
Miftah separates access by organisation,
role, and property assignment.

2
00:00:03,474 --> 00:00:07,720
This tutorial shows how those boundaries
shape the interface, and why

3
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:11,966
a missing menu is usually correct
behaviour rather than an error.

4
00:00:11,966 --> 00:00:13,896
Start as the System Admin.

5
00:00:13,896 --> 00:00:17,756
The role is shown under the name, and the
organisation

6
00:00:17,756 --> 00:00:21,616
switcher at the top of the side panel
reads Administering.

7
00:00:21,616 --> 00:00:22,388
Open it.

8
00:00:22,388 --> 00:00:27,020
A System Admin can work in Global View or
inside one organisation,

9
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:31,267
here Oasis Crest Properties, which is
ticked as the active one.

10
00:00:31,267 --> 00:00:35,127
Switching organisation never copies or
merges records between organisations, so

11
00:00:35,127 --> 00:00:35,513
always

12
00:00:35,513 --> 00:00:39,759
check the name here before you create,
edit, or delete anything.

13
00:00:39,759 --> 00:00:41,303
Next, the Company Admin.

14
00:00:41,303 --> 00:00:43,619
This role runs one organisation: its

15
00:00:43,619 --> 00:00:45,935
portfolio, leasing, collections,
accounting, and settings.

16
00:00:45,935 --> 00:00:46,707
Open Settings.

17
00:00:46,707 --> 00:00:50,181
The Company Admin sees Organisation, Users
and staff, Rent

18
00:00:50,181 --> 00:00:53,655
and fines, and Payments, but not the
Administration section,

19
00:00:53,655 --> 00:00:57,129
with Organisations and Users, that the
System Admin has.

20
00:00:57,129 --> 00:00:58,673
Now the Property Manager.

21
00:00:58,673 --> 00:01:02,533
The rail has no Settings, and Properties
lists only the

22
00:01:02,533 --> 00:01:06,007
property assigned to this manager, Oasis
Crest Residence Tower.

23
00:01:06,007 --> 00:01:09,867
Opening the address of an unassigned
property directly does not

24
00:01:09,867 --> 00:01:13,727
get around that: Miftah reports that the
property was not

25
00:01:13,727 --> 00:01:17,587
found, or that you may not have access to
it.

26
00:01:17,587 --> 00:01:18,745
Next, the Tenant.

27
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:21,833
A tenant signs in to the Tenant Portal,

28
00:01:21,833 --> 00:01:24,921
with their tenancy contracts, payments,
penalties, tickets, listings,

29
00:01:24,921 --> 00:01:28,009
and meetings, and none of the internal
administration.

30
00:01:28,009 --> 00:01:32,255
Two more roles are described in Help,
under Roles and Permissions.

31
00:01:32,255 --> 00:01:36,502
A Company User has limited access, to
their assigned unit details.

32
00:01:36,502 --> 00:01:39,590
A Security Guard manages gate access at
assigned

33
00:01:39,590 --> 00:01:42,292
properties, scanning passes and handling
approved visitors.

34
00:01:42,292 --> 00:01:46,152
Finish back as the System Admin: open the
switcher and

35
00:01:46,152 --> 00:01:50,012
confirm that Oasis Crest Properties is
still the active organisation.

36
00:01:50,012 --> 00:01:51,942
The safe habit is simple.

37
00:01:51,942 --> 00:01:54,644
Check the organisation, the role, and the

38
00:01:54,644 --> 00:01:56,960
property assignment before every sensitive
action.

39
00:01:56,960 --> 00:02:00,820
If access looks wrong, do not borrow a
broader account;

40
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:04,680
ask an administrator to correct the role
or the assignment.
